#
# Worked example — path-relative holonic levels and the materialized min/max depth
# band (ME9, issue #775).
#
# Holarchies are DAGs, not ladders: an entity can be a proper part of several wholes
# along several paths, so it has NO single intrinsic "level." A level is meaningful
# only relative to a path. This file materializes that band for one DAG node.
#
# The DAG (a diamond — ex:Sensor has TWO parents, ex:Wing directly and via ex:Avionics):
#
#     ex:Aircraft
#        | properPartOf
#       ex:Wing  ◄───────────────┐
#        |                        |
#     ex:Avionics                 |  (ex:Sensor is ALSO a direct proper part of ex:Wing)
#        |                        |
#      ex:Sensor  ────────────────┘
#       /   \
#  ex:ChipA  ex:ChipB
#
# ex:Sensor occupies TWO logic:HolonicPositions, one per path, each the canonical
# five-place construct (entity, holarchy, context, interval, path) and each carrying
# its own logic:holonicLevel — a literal READ OFF the position (rdfs:domain
# logic:HolonicPosition), never an intrinsic attribute of the entity:
#
#   * ex:posSensorDirect  path ex:pathDirect            → logic:holonicLevel 1
#   * ex:posSensorVia     path ex:pathVia (via Avionics) → logic:holonicLevel 2
#
# Both readings are correct. The per-entity min/max band over those positions is
# materialized on the entity:
#
#   * ex:Sensor logic:holonicLevelMin 1 ; logic:holonicLevelMax 2 .
#
# HONEST SCOPE (#775): the band endpoints are operator-asserted, NOT engine-derived.
# The foundation chase is all-IRI (logic:StratifiedNAFProfile) and cannot compare or
# aggregate the integer levels, so it grounds only that the band EXISTS — via the
# derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (ex:Sensor occupies two distinct positions).
# That engine-verified structure is the companion conformance case
# conformance/logic/cases/holonic/holonic-band, which is IRI-only (the evaluator
# rejects literal objects); this file carries the literal band the chase cannot hold.
# See design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/> .

# The holarchy and its strict-parthood diamond.
ex:bandHolarchy a logic:Holarchy .

ex:ChipA    logic:properPartOf ex:Sensor .
ex:ChipB    logic:properPartOf ex:Sensor .
ex:Sensor   logic:properPartOf ex:Wing .
ex:Sensor   logic:properPartOf ex:Avionics .
ex:Avionics logic:properPartOf ex:Wing .
ex:Wing     logic:properPartOf ex:Aircraft .

# ex:Sensor is a holon along two paths through the holarchy.
ex:posSensorDirect
    a logic:HolonicPosition ;
    logic:positionEntity   ex:Sensor ;
    logic:positionHolarchy ex:bandHolarchy ;
    logic:positionContext  ex:OperationalContext ;
    logic:positionInterval ex:MissionInterval ;
    logic:positionPath     ex:pathDirect ;
    logic:holonicLevel     "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .

ex:posSensorVia
    a logic:HolonicPosition ;
    logic:positionEntity   ex:Sensor ;
    logic:positionHolarchy ex:bandHolarchy ;
    logic:positionContext  ex:OperationalContext ;
    logic:positionInterval ex:MissionInterval ;
    logic:positionPath     ex:pathVia ;
    logic:holonicLevel     "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .

# The materialized per-entity depth band over ex:Sensor's positions.
ex:Sensor
    logic:holonicLevelMin "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    logic:holonicLevelMax "2"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger .
